WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:06.730
This story is one that lightly describes the ordinary daily lives of the three Minami sisters.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:09.340
Please don't expect too much from it.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:11.300
Also, watch in a bright room,

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.990
and stay 3 meters away from the TV while watching.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:22.370
Kana

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:22.710
Chiaki

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:23.500
Haruka

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:50.040
Love Going Around in Circles

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:58.930
So, what's this?

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:02.130
Obviously, this is what you wear during New Year's Day.

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:04.130
Incidentally, the men's clothing belongs to Makoto.

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:05.210
Yup!

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:07.370
The kimono is Uchida's.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:10.850
When you think of Japanese people, you think of traditional clothes.

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:12.850
And New Year's Day is about the kimono.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:15.030
That's common knowledge in Japan.

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:26.050
And so, today we shall hold a rehearsal for the upcoming New Year's Day.

00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:30.020
Rehearsal?

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.300
Come, wear this.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:43.490
There's no way I could wear such flamboyant clothes!

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:49.020
Even with a kimono like this, I can't hide my manly Japanese spirit!

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:50.560
It suits you!

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:53.970
Okay! Touma is next!

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:55.920
Yeah. Is this okay?

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:00.600
Can you not see this cherry blossom storm?

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:03.960
Hey, Touma.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:06.290
I understand your enthusiasm,

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:09.870
But there is something you need more of right now.

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:13.090
A sense of shame.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.860
Your opinion, Uchida?

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:23.750
Yes, it'd be regretful if it were my first time meeting her.

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:25.310
In a good sense.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:26.540
Same sentiments.

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:28.060
Then, what about this here?

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:33.150
Yes, it'd be regretful if it were my first time meeting him.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.680
In a bad sense.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.230
Same sentiments.

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:38.230
In a bad sense?

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:40.100
But rest assured.

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:42.900
I'm sure Haruka will tell you that you're cute.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:45.260
Eh? Haruka-san will?

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:51.390
In any case, we can celebrate New Year's like this.

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:54.290
Hello!

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:56.980
Oh, Yoshino! You're late.

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:59.710
We're already in New Year mood here.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:02.970
The clothes suit the two of you!

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:04.140
Yep!

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:05.090
You can depend on me!

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:16.520
When a girl wears a kimono, she should take off her underwear, if I remember correctly?

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:22.510
That's what my mother told me.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:25.490
She said that's the customary way of wearing a kimono.

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:30.120
<i>I'm sure Haruka will tell you that you're cute.</i>

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:32.960
<i>...Tell you that you're cute.</i>

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.060
<i>...That you're cute.</i>

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:35.920
<i>So cute!
...That you're cute.</i>

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:38.920
No!

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:41.900
Don't stop me, Uchida!

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:44.970
That's right. Taking off the underwear is the customary way!

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:46.970
You can't do that even it's the customary way!

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:51.310
So Mako-chan's kimono belongs to Uchida!

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:57.520
I can't believe that one sentence could cause this interesting turn of events!

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:00.020
Way to go, Yoshino.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:01.780
Minami-ke!

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:10.790
How about calling him now?

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:11.980
A call to Fujioka-kun.

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:15.080
I need to be mentally prepared...

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.170
You're inviting him to a New Year shrine visit, aren't you?

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:21.050
If you don't get a confirmation from him soon, he might have other plans.

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:22.410
Other plans?

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:25.050
Kana...

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:27.770
No! Not Kana!

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:31.010
Like his family, or soccer club members, right?

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:32.930
Y-You're right.

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:38.380
Yes. Look, this is Fujioka-kun's phone number.

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:44.240
Excuse me. That's mine.

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:51.580
Hello. Kana?

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:52.870
What's the matter?

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:54.500
Fujioka-kun.

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:08.090
Minami's talking to someone else?

00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:18.520
Let me practice one more time.

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:22.440
Hello, my name is Fujioka. Is Minami-san...

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:27.350
Aren't Haruka-san and Chiaki-chan called Minami as well?

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:33.830
My name is Fujioka. Is Kana-san...

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:36.880
Is "-san" a bit too formal?

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:41.000
<i>League champion.</i>

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:43.960
<i>Champion.</i>

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:46.670
<i>Chan.</i>

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:54.210
Ka... Ka-Ka-Ka-Ka... Kana!... -chan.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.560
Let's go with Kana-san.

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:10.410
Which means, because you got a hundred marks for your test,

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:12.620
They bought you a cell phone?

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.680
Yeah, that's right.

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:16.500
I was wrong about you, Keiko.

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:20.860
I thought you'd be the last person to do this sort of thing.

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:22.710
Eh? What do you...

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:25.870
It's true that you're better at studying than others.

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:27.870
Everytime you're asked how many points you got,

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:30.720
You always say "a hundred percent" with a smile on your face.

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:34.000
I don't think I always smile when doing that.

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:37.800
Oh? Which means you don't deny the part about the "hundred percent"?

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:42.300
Look, Keiko, what does a hundred marks mean?

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:49.620
Isn't a hundred marks to us students an honor that can't be replaced with anything else?

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:52.830
I don't think it's such a big deal...

00:07:53.660 --> 00:08:00.120
But Keiko, you got a cell phone in return for getting a hundred percent.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:01.870
Which means to say...

00:08:03.260 --> 00:08:06.040
Because you want the cell phone, the honor of getting a hundred percent...

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:08.310
You sold your soul as a student!

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:10.050
Your hundred marks are filthy!

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:16.540
I wonder who Keiko is talking to.

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:21.730
I should be able to get through now.

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:27.290
He's still using the phone.

00:08:27.290 --> 00:08:29.270
She's still using the phone?

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:36.840
One more time!

00:08:37.570 --> 00:08:38.960
One more time!

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:49.210
Could she have hung up the receiver?

00:08:52.830 --> 00:08:53.920
Wow...

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:56.040
A cell phone really is convenient.

00:08:56.040 --> 00:09:00.890
Yup. But if you don't keep track, your phone bill will skyrocket.

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:03.350
A cell phone's phone bill...

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:05.140
Is that expensive?

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:08.390
It won't be if you don't use it for a long time.

00:09:08.390 --> 00:09:11.630
Speaking of which, we have been talking for a long time now.

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:13.370
Ah, yeah.

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:17.950
It's already 4pm, so we've been talking for two hours now.

00:09:19.610 --> 00:09:20.970
Two hours?

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:23.850
Isn't that hard on the phone bill?

00:09:24.970 --> 00:09:29.130
Since you called me, the phone bill's on you.

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:31.390
Stop screwing with me!

00:09:31.390 --> 00:09:33.260
You filthy hundred-mark monster!

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:39.300
Filthy... hundred-mark...

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:42.260
I can't get through...

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:45.450
Which means I'm the only one who can't get connected...

00:09:45.450 --> 00:09:47.180
He has my number blacklisted.

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:52.040
Perhaps I should have invited her before the winter vacation started.

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:53.320
For the shrine visit.

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:58.820
If I go to the shrine, I might run into her, right?

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:02.770
Oh, that's right, Kana.

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:06.630
You were on the phone the whole day, weren't you?

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:09.040
You shouldn't use the phone too much.

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:12.640
Exactly. Don't put any more stress on Haruka-neesama.

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:14.760
She's the one who has to keep track of the house expenses.

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:17.340
Give the phone bill to Keiko!

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:20.560
This is the billing address!

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:24.180
Thanks for the food.

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:39.900
<b>Soba Noodles Restaurant:
Yasuda</b>

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:40.070
New Year's Eve Soba Noodles
<b>Soba Noodles Restaurant:
Yasuda</b>

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:43.410
New Year's Eve Soba Noodles

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:47.260
New Year's Eve on a Luxurious Liner Chapter
Hosaka's Simulated Fantasy

00:11:58.780 --> 00:11:59.690
Yasuda

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:09.270
I came to be by your side.

00:12:18.350 --> 00:12:19.790
One order for handmade buckwheat noodles!

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:22.150
This is mine!

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:24.760
Instant noodles are good enough for you!

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:29.540
The bells for New Year haven't rung yet, my daughters.

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:47.860
Hey, Natsuki-kun.

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:49.070
Yes?

00:12:49.070 --> 00:12:52.220
The part-timer Hosaka-kun who you brought along today...

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:55.020
Why is he making soba noodles on his own?

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:56.830
He's doing it for the woman he loves.

00:12:56.830 --> 00:13:00.330
No, that's not what I meant...

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:03.260
Does he need any other reason for doing so?

00:13:06.690 --> 00:13:07.760
No...

00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:11.180
You're doing well, Senpai.

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:13.760
Natsuki, huh? I give you my thanks.

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:15.760
You've introduced me to a good shop.

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:19.030
Not at all. I'm glad to be of help to you.

00:13:19.030 --> 00:13:21.800
So, were you able to make something you're happy with?

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:24.030
Yeah. Try it.

00:13:25.510 --> 00:13:26.900
I'm digging in.

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:35.850
<i>This rich and invigorating aroma that's wafting through my nostrils.</i>

00:13:35.850 --> 00:13:40.040
<i>With one mouthful, I can picture in my mind Senpai preparing this.</i>

00:13:40.830 --> 00:13:42.800
<i>What a wonderful taste!</i>

00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:44.450
<i>But...</i>

00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:45.570
How do you find it?

00:13:45.570 --> 00:13:46.720
Wonderful as I'd expect.

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:48.250
I see.

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:50.320
But I don't understand.

00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:53.730
60 percent, no, it's 80, isn't it?

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:56.390
Besides buckwheat flour, you've also added wheat flour.

00:13:56.970 --> 00:14:01.360
With your skills, you should be able to use 100 percent buckwheat flour.

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:02.390
Indeed.

00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:05.280
May I know the reason?

00:14:06.250 --> 00:14:10.090
It's obvious that by using only buckwheat flour, I achieve the true flavor of buckwheat noodles.

00:14:10.090 --> 00:14:12.820
Noodles of utmost perfection.

00:14:12.820 --> 00:14:18.000
But because of that, the person tasting it would become needlessly tensed up.

00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:23.250
I believe that a meal should be something that brings peace to the heart.

00:14:23.990 --> 00:14:26.750
And I believe the girls feel the same way too.

00:14:29.320 --> 00:14:31.530
Am I being too naïve?

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:32.740
Not at all.

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:34.740
That's not naïve.

00:14:35.650 --> 00:14:37.180
It's tenderness.

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:40.480
Well then, I'll get going now.

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:41.990
I wish you a good year ahead.

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:45.100
Where's he going?

00:14:46.140 --> 00:14:49.280
<i>Senpai, I wish you the best of luck.</i>

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:52.240
Last Episode 10 Hour Special
Sensei and Ninomiya-kun

00:14:56.690 --> 00:14:58.150
Farewell, Sensei!

00:14:58.150 --> 00:15:00.660
Please forget me!

00:15:00.660 --> 00:15:03.370
What nonsense are you talking about? Ninomiya-kun!

00:15:05.290 --> 00:15:07.730
Come over here, Ninomiya-kun.

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:09.230
Don't come any closer, Sensei!

00:15:12.500 --> 00:15:14.360
Great, the car's gone.

00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:14.740
Ninomiya-

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:17.590
Nooooo!

00:15:17.590 --> 00:15:19.540
Ninomiya-kun!

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:21.080
Ah, that's a stunt doll.

00:15:23.960 --> 00:15:26.500
Begin with a rock, Rock, Paper, Scissors!

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:28.620
Damn it!

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:29.910
Yo!

00:15:29.910 --> 00:15:32.010
Oh! Good evening!

00:15:32.010 --> 00:15:33.820
These are presents.

00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:36.340
Thank you, thank you!

00:15:36.340 --> 00:15:37.220
It's heavy!

00:15:37.220 --> 00:15:39.550
These are imported top-grade juices.

00:15:39.550 --> 00:15:41.870
Let's drink the night away!

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:43.830
No alcohol for minors.

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:45.320
Yo!

00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:47.320
Hayami-senpai! Welcome!

00:15:47.320 --> 00:15:49.170
You're watching Ninomiya-kun?

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:51.300
Let's watch "The Macho Hunks" instead.

00:15:52.070 --> 00:15:54.130
What time are you going for the New Year shrine visit?

00:15:54.130 --> 00:15:56.630
Let's decide that after Maki and the rest arrive.

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:02.290
All these juices look suspicious.

00:16:11.420 --> 00:16:14.030
Chiaki should be fine with carbonated ones.

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:16.450
Alright, shall we begin?

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:17.280
Okay!

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:20.660
Then, everyone, congratulations on all your hard work this year!

00:16:21.070 --> 00:16:23.170
Congratulations!

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:31.480
Water, water!

00:16:31.480 --> 00:16:34.340
Hey, what's wrong with this juice?

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:36.020
It's imported.

00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:40.000
Imported? What's this taste?

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:46.120
Haruka-neesama, there's a mountain of suspicious and poisonous-looking juice in the kitchen.

00:16:47.180 --> 00:16:48.560
Let's play a game.

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:51.560
He's running, he's running! The Loincloth Man!

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:54.320
There he goes!

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:56.570
Go! Deal the final blow!

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:58.230
In one shot! Yes, that's right!

00:16:58.670 --> 00:17:02.200
Oh! The Loincloth Man on the red side used foul play!

00:17:02.590 --> 00:17:05.450
Using the loincloth to strangle the opponent? A cowardly act!

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:07.190
What are you doing?!

00:17:07.190 --> 00:17:08.670
Run away, run away!

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:09.780
Run away!

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:11.870
That's the end of Round One.

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:18.560
Next. Haruka-chan, put your left hand on a blue spot.

00:17:18.560 --> 00:17:20.770
My left hand...

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:22.010
On a blue spot...

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:32.730
Yay! Both of you lose!

00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:35.900
That's because Kana just...

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:38.070
Oh! Sorry!

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:40.030
Don't apologize in English!

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:43.390
Okay, okay! Since the two of you lost, strip!

00:17:44.530 --> 00:17:47.710
Or else, have some juice!

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:53.170
Kana, what are you doing with that camera?

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:55.790
I'm thinking about leaving behind some fun memories.

00:18:01.040 --> 00:18:04.280
Come, the game has just begun!

00:18:05.510 --> 00:18:08.180
The official rule states five three-minute rounds!

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:10.680
No way!

00:18:13.910 --> 00:18:17.620
The two sides never give up and the battle has finally entered the last round.

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:20.690
This fight's getting more intense.

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:23.610
Go, go!

00:18:23.610 --> 00:18:25.220
Left! More to the left!

00:18:25.220 --> 00:18:27.220
Use more power on the left!

00:18:33.590 --> 00:18:34.920
All of you.

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:37.360
It's already this late, so you'd better keep quiet.

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:41.950
Haruka-neesama's scary!

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:44.870
<i>Who the hell are you two?</i>

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:48.790
Huh? I'm... scary?

00:18:48.790 --> 00:18:51.030
Like a demon!

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:57.480
No way! You're mean!

00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:00.980
She fell asleep.

00:19:00.980 --> 00:19:03.900
Neesama... Neesama, where are you?

00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:05.700
She's on the opposite side.

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:07.910
Neesama... Neesama!

00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:15.830
I can't believe Haruka and Chiaki are this broken.

00:19:15.830 --> 00:19:17.330
Does it really taste good?

00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:18.860
It's top-grade, after all.

00:19:21.420 --> 00:19:23.340
Good evening.

00:19:24.610 --> 00:19:27.340
Let the two sleeping dogs lie.

00:19:27.340 --> 00:19:31.120
Master, give these two the twister game, and this as well!

00:19:31.120 --> 00:19:32.560
Yes sir!

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:38.480
Is it really, really tasty?

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:40.220
It's juice after all.

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:45.860
Let's go visit the shrine!

00:19:51.890 --> 00:19:53.650
Everyone's unconscious.

00:19:53.650 --> 00:19:54.950
Is that so?

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:57.810
I guess we went a bit too far!

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:07.430
Let's go somewhere nice, just the two of us.

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:11.680
<i>This person is the most broken of them all!</i>

00:20:11.680 --> 00:20:15.950
Senpai! That juice is actually nasty, isn't it?

00:20:15.950 --> 00:20:17.720
It's imported goods, after all.

00:20:17.720 --> 00:20:20.020
You've been forcing yourself to drink it, haven't you?

00:20:20.020 --> 00:20:21.690
It's top-grade, after all.

00:20:21.690 --> 00:20:23.850
You don't have to force yourself to drink it!

00:20:23.850 --> 00:20:25.500
I paid for it myself, after all!

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:44.260
We're finally married, Ninomiya-kun.

00:20:44.650 --> 00:20:45.710
Sensei!

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:03.320
No!

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:04.820
Save me!

00:21:04.820 --> 00:21:06.590
Haruka, Haruka!

00:21:06.590 --> 00:21:08.150
Chia... Chiaki!

00:21:17.370 --> 00:21:19.370
Where is the Minami Residence?

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:26.750
Minami Haruka.

00:21:26.750 --> 00:21:31.310
You're somewhere among those lights, listening to the ringing of the New Year Bells, aren't you?

00:21:31.310 --> 00:21:32.860
That's good enough for me.

00:21:32.860 --> 00:21:37.020
Laughing with your family in a cozy room, awaiting the arrival of the New Year.

00:21:37.470 --> 00:21:40.190
That's what happiness is about.

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:44.310
Come! New Year's Eve noodles for four!
